.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-record-forge 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-record\-forge \- Record the forge\*(Aqs check verdicts for one commit, read as `<check> <conclusion>` lines on stdin or with \-\-fetch from the forge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten record forge\fR [\fB\-\-fetch\fR] [\fB\-\-fanin\fR] [\fB\-\-answered\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIref\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record the forge\*(Aqs check verdicts for one commit, read as `<check> <conclusion>` lines on stdin or with \-\-fetch from the forge
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fetch\fR
Read the commit\*(Aqs check\-runs from the forge instead of `<check> <conclusion>` lines on stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-fanin\fR \fI<fanin>\fR
With \-\-fetch: record nothing until this check has an answered conclusion
.TP
\fB\-\-answered\fR \fI<answered>\fR
With \-\-fetch: comma\-separated conclusions that constitute an answer; anything else is not recorded
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIref\fR>
The ref or sha the verdict was taken against
